{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153938-showcase-your-supernal-entities-goetia-spirits-and-ghosts-homebrew","id":1153938,"title":"Showcase your Supernal Entities, Goetia, Spirits and Ghosts (Homebrew)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-29T10:21:30-07:00","id":1153938,"title":"Showcase your Supernal Entities, Goetia, Spirits and Ghosts (Homebrew)","content":"I don't yet have anything to contribute to the topic, but I figured that if people could make example spells, then why not homebrew spirits, Goetia, and all of the various things out there. I know that any Storyteller has probably had to build their own for each of these beings and more, so I figure there's probably a lot of untapped potential waiting out there, and especially when it comes to Goetia and Supernal Entities, there's definitely a lot more examples that we could use. (Summoners is great, but it's both not 2e, and clearly meant to provide only a small sample of what you could create. <br /> <br /> I do plan to contribute to this topic myself at some point, I'm currently working on some Supernal Entities, but I don't have anything yet.<br /> <br /> So have at ye?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T11:05:34-07:00","id":1153944,"title":"","content":"<b>Perpetuus:</b> A Rank 6 goetia. Perpetuus is the manifest dream of the concept of causality. He resides in a spiral tower in the Sidereal Wastes, located on the astral reflection of Saturn's moon Phoebe. He was primarily a plot device used for some characters who died (almost, but not quite) get their bodies back by rewriting time. His primary Numen is a Lasting version of the Rewrite History spell. The trick is that he has a price, which is to take part of your own history away. What he does with these collected bits of history is anyone's guess. Mechanically, this is represented by shifting merits and skills around<br /> <br /> <b>The Narrow Path:</b> A Rank 4 Supernal Entity representing the cycle of Life through mass extinction events. Thrown out of the Primal Wilds by the Exarchs long ago, it now lies slumbering somewhere on the edges of the Anima Mundi. When it stirs, ecosystems start to collapse. Ban: The Narrow Path cannot harm anyone who possesses teeth or claws from the 5 greatest predators of each era it ended with a mass extinction event. Bane: A weapon owned by someone who personally killed at least 100 people in a genocide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T09:03:42-07:00","id":1155085,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Wraith of Eyes&quot;: A Rank 2 Supernal Entity. A Demon of Mind, its trial involves viewing sights and sounds designed to make one cry out or break, from the lives of people who died, or who faced great adversity. If one can stand up to it without breaking, one can gain its boon. The thing most Mages summon it for is that it allows them to view the world out of the eyes of someone else for a time... literally, in this case. It can allow you to know what your enemy is up to even if you don't have the skill at Space, or the sympathetic connection, to view him more directly. The peeks it gives are only brief, and relate to what the target is doing at the time, thus making it an entity one summons with great care towards the timing. After all, you wouldn't want to merely see the inside of someone's eyelids, would you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","user":"The_Laurent","date":". 11-02-2017, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T11:29:44-07:00","id":1155143,"title":"","content":"Would need to be Rank 2 to access Scrying, but a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T11:31:59-07:00","id":1155145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153938-showcase-your-supernal-entities-goetia-spirits-and-ghosts-homebrew?p=1155143#post1155143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would need to be Rank 2 to access Scrying, but a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fixed it. Though now I'm wondering what sorts of things you summon a Rank 1 Supernal Entity for. But yeah, Mind 2, Space 2, potentially other stuff at ST allowance, though Mind is the primary, and it's why it is a Wraith rather than an Imp. It's about seeing through the mind's eye, and thus merely uses Space, rather than being *about* Space like an Imp might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T12:17:38-07:00","id":1155159,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">This is the ghost of the infamous judge who presided over the Salem witch trials, but possessed by a diabolic Inferno lower depths demon. In my game the Tremere left him in charge of Danvers Asylum when they abandoned it:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Jonathan Hathorne</b> (Possessed by a Larval Diabolic Demon - Infernal Rank 3)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Attributes: Power 7, Finesse 5, Resistance 7<br /> Willpower: 14<br /> Morality: 1 (Megalomania)<br /> Virtue: Justice<br /> Vice: Greed<br /> Initiative: 12<br /> Defense: 7<br /> Speed: 22 (species factor 10)<br /> Size: 5<br /> Corpus: 12<br /> Essence: 30</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Numina: Clairvoyance (dice pool 12), Compulsion (dice pool 12), Ghost Sign (dice pool 12), Ghost Speech (dice pool 12), Magnetic Disruption, Phantasm (dice pool 12), Possession (dice pool 12), Telekinesis (dice pool 12), Terrify (dice pool 12), Greater Hellform<br /> <br /> \u2022 Greater Hellform: Unnatural speed and strange limbs allow it to make an additional attack for every dot of Finesse over 3. Storytellers may also divide its Infernal Rank between bonus attack dice and Corpus. Roll Power + Resistance. Each success allows the demon to maintain the Hellform for a turn. This Numen costs 1 Willpower (which does not add 3 dice to any actions) to activate, plus 1 point of Essence for every turn it functions.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Arm Ghost: Entropic Shield 5, Mind Shield 4, Magic Shield 3, Restore Corpus, Counterspell</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Use the full range of his abilities to set up a truly terrifying encounter.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T13:39:08-07:00","id":1155178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153938-showcase-your-supernal-entities-goetia-spirits-and-ghosts-homebrew?p=1155143#post1155143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would need to be Rank 2 to access Scrying, but a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be the function of a Numen rather than the use of an Arcanum &quot;Influence&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T18:07:58-07:00","id":1155234,"title":"","content":"I did have another idea, though I'm not sure what the secondary Arcana would be (it's either Fate or Time), or the specifics of how it'd work. <br /> <br /> Another, the Revealer of Ways: It shows what one was, and what one can be. By challenging a Mage on the choices they made in the past, and the ways they could have been, their trial dares them to try to 'change' things, but those Mages who do fail. Only those who accept that they are themselves can then gain the primary thing that Another can do. While they can serve as a handy guide to the immediate past, and the skein of fate, what they do most of all is show a person who they could have been if they made other choices. Or if others in their life (such as parents) had acted differently. By viewing these different selves, a Mage might obsess over what they did wrong... or learn to accept that this life and these choices are the ones they made. <br /> <br /> (Probably can serve as a source of Conditions/XP, not sure.)<br /> <br /> (I just like the idea of showing alternate selves of a person, or the idea of what they'd be like, to taunt and challenge a Mage.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T19:06:43-07:00","id":1155248,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\">Here</a> you have some examples already, feel free to add there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T06:25:16-07:00","id":1155712,"title":"","content":"<b>The Womb:</b> A Rank 4 Entity, The Womb is one of the many Supernal reflections of the Concept of monstrous fertilities. When Summoned, it doesn't take a form on its own: instead, it takes over even the tiniest bits of organical matter inside and around her Summoning Circle, using his Supernal Powers to make them evolve in progressively stranger and more complex organisms, all meant as biological murder machines, full of claws and fangs and unnaturally placed appendages. Said offspring starts fighting against every other living organism they see: at first, that includes one another, but soon enough, an alpha, the most refined predator born of the Womb, takes their lead and organized slaughter ensues. If the summoner manages to tame, kill, or otherwise asserting its dominance over this alpha, he wins the Trial: the Womb stops its production, but its progeny remains under his command for the Duration of the Entity's stay in the Fallen World. The subtelty of the Trial is to wait long enough to let the Womb develop the most evolved (and therefore useful) progeny as possible... while not succumbing against the increasingly lethal horde.<br /> <br /> <b>The Harem:</b> A remote cousin of the Womb (if such familial analogy holds when it comes down to Supernal Denizens), the Harem is another Rank 4 Supernal Entity, this time a Wraith stemming from Pandemonium. Called upon by Mastigos well versed in the Mind and Life Arcana, it appears as a group of strikingly beautiful subjects. As soon as the Harem enters the Fallen World, each of its iteration will engage one bystander (including the Summoner) in Social Maneuvering, with the objective \u201cLead that person to betray her own objectives or ties of loyalty\u201d. The summoner\u2019s gambit is that his Mastigos self-control will be enough to keep the temptation at bay longer than his enemies. Usually, that suffices. Usually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 11-06-2017, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T12:04:08-08:00","id":1156112,"title":"","content":"<b>Autocide:</b> A Rank 3 Moira from Arcadia, wielding Death and Fate (or maybe a Wraith with Death and Mind... not sure yet).<br /> <br /> Autocide appears like an extremely cheerful nurse, usually with a mug of coffee in one hand and a joint in the other: when she laughs - which she does often-, her squinted eyes flash with a silvery gleam. Contrarily to many Entities, Autocide doesn't draw a clear line between its Trial and its services: its abilities are both a gift and curse, and simply requiring her to perform them implies that the Summoner is ready to stomach the consequence.<br /> <br /> Autocide is only Summoned to one desperate purpose: fake one's death, Whether by using Death to give to the mage's body the appearance of a corpse, or Fate to allow him to survive a lethal event unbeknowst to anyone else. The Catch ? Autocide will also manage to make everyone <i>happy </i>about it. All those who acknowledge the Summoner's death (and particularly those who loved him and were loved by him) will be showered in Boons and other positive Fate effects, meant to make them thinking of that loss as the best thing that ever happened to them: or, at least, make them forget the &quot;deceased&quot; altogether. The Summoner will have to witness that happiness, and choose: either breaking it through resurfacing (proving that he deliberately lied about his death), or cut the ties. Unless he also becomes convinces that everyone would be happier without him, and decides to really kill himself...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T08:21:28-08:00","id":1158952,"title":"","content":"No spirits, huh? Let's get a spirit in here.<br /> <br /> <b>Watches In Silence</b> - a Rank 5 spirit of a city's university. Originally it was (and for the most part is still) a spirit of information, feeding on the knowledge generated by the students, professors, and researchers that studied and taught at the university. Such institutions contain plenty of books, computers, academic papers stored physically or electronically, and other forms of information.<br /> During the early days of the university, Watches In Silence began as a spirit of a book. As the university grew, the spirit fed on other spirits of the court of knowledge - later becoming the spirit of the library, and later becoming the spirit of the university at rank 4.<br /> However, as Watches In Silence grows to represent the university at large, and as more and more spirits of the courts of emotion and ideology become fat off of the stress and ideological stances of those who study and teach - Watches In Silence has begun to feed off the negative emotions and ideologies, for how easy is it to disguise an ideology as fact - or belief as knowledge? <br /> <br /> Rank 5<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Attributes: Power 15, Finesse 12, Resistance 14<br /> Willpower: 10 (max for spirits ranked 1-5)<br /> Initiative: 26<br /> Defense: 12<br /> Speed: 27 (species factor 0)<br /> Size: 5<br /> Corpus: 19<br /> Essence: 50<br /> <br /> Bane - the original manuscript of an academic paper covering scientific research. It must be authored solely by professors (and their students) who worked at the university during its first 10 years. In modern days, this may refer to the first printout of such a paper that matches the published version - often printed by the professor for proofreading.<br /> <br /> Ban - Watches In Silence cannot harm, influence, or otherwise compel a high ranked member of the university's administrative branches - including deans, program directors, presidents, and other administrative branches. It's attacks do not harm any such administrator, and it cannot grapple them either. It is also unable to target them with any of its numina, influences, or manifestations, but it can feed off of their resonance.<br /> <br /> Influences - Information 4, Extremism 1, Stress 1<br /> <br /> Manifestations - Twilight Form, Discorporate, Reaching, Image, Fetter, Possess</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Numina (dice pool 27): Aggressive Meme, Dement, Emotional Aura, Implant Mission, Innocuous, Left-Handed Spanner, Mortal Mask, Pathfinder, Sign, Telekinesis</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21757-oeruli","user":"oeruli","date":".  Modified ban to apply to high ranked administrators instead of tenured STEM professors. Note some professors still count for this ban. 11-15-2017, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21757-oeruli","name":"oeruli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T08:36:22-08:00","id":1158960,"title":"","content":"I like it, but it would have to be a really influential university, perhaps even internationally famous to have its own Rank 5 spirit. You have any in mind, real or invented?<br /> <br /> Also, why only STEM professors? Why not historians or music professors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T08:39:23-08:00","id":1158961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153938-showcase-your-supernal-entities-goetia-spirits-and-ghosts-homebrew?p=1156112#post1156112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Autocide:</b> A Rank 3 Moira from Arcadia, wielding Death and Fate (or maybe a Wraith with Death and Mind... not sure yet).<br /> <br /> Autocide appears like an extremely cheerful nurse, usually with a mug of coffee in one hand and a joint in the other: when she laughs - which she does often-, her squinted eyes flash with a silvery gleam. Contrarily to many Entities, Autocide doesn't draw a clear line between its Trial and its services: its abilities are both a gift and curse, and simply requiring her to perform them implies that the Summoner is ready to stomach the consequence.<br /> <br /> Autocide is only Summoned to one desperate purpose: fake one's death, Whether by using Death to give to the mage's body the appearance of a corpse, or Fate to allow him to survive a lethal event unbeknowst to anyone else. The Catch ? Autocide will also manage to make everyone <i>happy </i>about it. All those who acknowledge the Summoner's death (and particularly those who loved him and were loved by him) will be showered in Boons and other positive Fate effects, meant to make them thinking of that loss as the best thing that ever happened to them: or, at least, make them forget the &amp;quot;deceased&amp;quot; altogether. The Summoner will have to witness that happiness, and choose: either breaking it through resurfacing (proving that he deliberately lied about his death), or cut the ties. Unless he also becomes convinces that everyone would be happier without him, and decides to really kill himself...</div> </div> </div> </div>I would just like to say i freaking love this. I could see someone use it if they were about to try some sort of die-or-fly ascension attempt","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T11:15:53-08:00","id":1159075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153938-showcase-your-supernal-entities-goetia-spirits-and-ghosts-homebrew?p=1158960#post1158960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it, but it would have to be a really influential university, perhaps even internationally famous to have its own Rank 5 spirit. You have any in mind, real or invented?<br /> <br /> Also, why only STEM professors? Why not historians or music professors?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you like it.<br /> <br /> 1. Indeed, it would have to be something along the lines of an ivy league university in the United States, or other well known universities such as Oxford or Cambridge - any internationally famous university as you pointed out. I didn't specify one so that it can be left open for use. It would certainly be appropriate to weaken it to rank 3 or 4 for less well known universities.<br /> <br /> 2. The bane and ban could also potentially be expanded to include all professors tenured at the university (I have a different idea I will discuss below). The main idea was to exclude political science professors. A professor of political science could easily be used as a tool to teach extremist ideals to impressionable students. Then again, anyone is open to stress, and anyone is open to extremist ideals. Any professor tenured at the university would make sense - it's hard enough to become a tenured professor as is.<br /> <br /> In retrospect, I think it makes more sense for the ban to apply to high ranked administrators of the university - deans, presidents, heads of administrative departments, etc. The purview of Watches In Silence is information and knowledge, as well as its transfer. The spirit could feed off of the sharing and teaching of information between professors and students, but would be at a loss with how to handle the administration. Professors are included in this, but not all professors - only professors with high ranked administrative rolls such as deans and program directors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21757-oeruli","name":"oeruli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T14:25:10-08:00","id":1159184,"title":"","content":"<b><u>The Scarlet Letter</u></b><br /> <br /> Don't be mislead by the Scarlet's Letter deceivingly small size: that Supernal Spirit is one of the most potent and frightful Wraiths in all Pandemonium. It embodies the social power that the outcast detains over those who shun them. The weight of a prostitute's glance on the men clamoring their disdain for her, but secretly lusting after her; the shame and cowardice they display while reluctantly bargaining with their drug dealer; the repressed admiration they feel when a foreigner (or a woman) turns out to perform better than the majority ; the fear in the heart of the righteous believers crossing the rumored witch's path, nervously gesturing in their pockets to conjure the evil eye.<br /> <br /> Rank: 5<br /> Arcana: Mind and Fate<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b><br /> Quite soberly, the Letter manifests as a doppelg\u00e4nger of its Summoner, standing quietly in its Summoner circle. The resemblance is perfect on every fashion \u2013 except for two things. First, its defiant, somber glare (in which some pretend to have seen fire, and ruins, and many other wonders. Second, the pattern of swollen, translucent veins it arbors on its forehead, or on the back of its left hand: the bloodflow, visibly coursing through them, traces the shape of the Scarlet Letter at each heartbeat.<br /> <br /> The Letter's form <i>per se</i> varies from one onlooker to another. Mages almost always see a twisted version of their Inferior Arcanum's Rune, while Vampires often see it take the shape of the number 7 (whatever that may mean, it doesn't seem to exactly please them). Only the strange creatures calling themselves &quot;Begotten&quot; seem thrilled by the sight of the Letter, enthusiastically refering to it as &quot;the Initial of the Dark Mother's Name&quot;. Mastigos know better than to inquire about that, but many shiver at the thought: if that is truly only the first letter, what in the <i>hell</i> (and for a Mastigos, Hell is meant quite literally) would answer to the full name?<br /> <br /> The Entity never try to communicate with its Summoner. When it answers to its Summoner's questions about his purviews, it's through telepathical imagery \u2013 often crude and traumatizing. The only occasions it\u2019ll express itself verbally is when he receives the order to use its powers against foes, or at the beginning of a fight where he and its Summoner will be involved. A simple phrase in High Speech, that one could translate as such: \u201cLet us be evil, then\u201d.<br /> <br /> <b>Trial: </b><br /> Summoning the Scarlet Letter is embracing the Outcast in oneself. It's becoming the villain, the monster extreme politicians paint in their hateful speeches, the Antichrist bigots yell about when they preach in the street, the opposite of what . The power of the Entity floods the body and soul of the Summoner, flailing him with all the bullying and exclusion he either suffered or inflicted, trying to tear apart the bastion of identity he built to be socially accepted: and the stronger that social stronghold is, the more painful that overthrowing shall be.<br /> <br /> Upon a successful evocation, the Summoner loses (Summoner's total Social Merit dots minus half their Gnosis) lethal damage. He can mitigate those injuries by accepting a -1 in any of his Resistance Attributes (Resolve, Stamina, Composure), on a 1-to-1 basis. It reflects the Entity's efforts to make him less thick-skinned, easier to alienate.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Power: Fueled by Their Fears</b><br /> <br /> Apart from his unparalleled mastery of both Mind and Fate Arcanum, as well as its extensive knowledge of all prosecuted/exiled/witch-hunted groups or individuals, the Scarlet Letter grants one quite peculiar boon: the power to pull his opponent\u2019s subconscious fears about the Other, and makes them true.<br /> <br /> The Summoner gains a pool of dices equal to his total Social Merits dots: in the unlikely case of a Summoner without any Social Merit dots, the pool contains (Gnosis minus the Summoner's lowest Social Attribute) dices. At any times while the Entity is less than 10 meters away from him, he may spend one dice, roll it and apply the effect specified next to its number (see below). He may spend 1 Mana to choose the entry directly above or below the one he rolled. If the pool is emptied, the Entity\u2019s time in the Fallen World is considered over, even if it shouldn\u2019t be over per usual Summoning rules. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">One</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">???</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Two</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">???</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Three</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">???</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Four</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">???</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Five</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">???</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Six</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">???</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Seven</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">???</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Eight</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">???</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Nine</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">???</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Ten</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">???</td> </tr> </table></div> (I'm trying to think of effects for &quot;Fueled By their Fears&quot;, but I thought it could be interesting to see what y'all guys thought about it. If you have some ideas, don't hesitate to propose!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 11-15-2017, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T14:27:43-08:00","id":1159187,"title":"","content":"You might consider integrating more the dark temptations of academia; the things that produce a cycle of self-expansion. The need for funding in academia is so dire that a 2017 Nobel Prize winner (Jeffrey Hall, whose work contributed to identifying circadian regulation mechanisms in flies, which were also found in people; a whole new model for understanding our body's regulatory systems) received his prize after he'd been forced to close his lab due to lack of funds.<br /> <br /> This is a feature the world over. The financial crisis crushed academic research funds, and they're slow to resurge, and this is hurt by the fact that equipment is increasingly expensive. A million dollars in funding might've been split between ten labs a few decades ago, but now it goes to one or two, both because of the relative expenses and the intricacies of scientific research in the modern era. <br /> <br /> As such, the temptation to fudge data or falsify findings or break ethics codes are getting all the stronger. Publish, as they say, or perish. A spirit definitely would want its university to grow, and so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T18:28:49-08:00","id":1159280,"title":"","content":"This is a good idea, Axelgear. Mechanically speaking, I think it could be done by taking the point of Extremism influence and moving it to either Information or Stress. Certainly this would be included among the many stresses of university life, but you do make a good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21757-oeruli","name":"oeruli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T02:24:08-08:00","id":1159753,"title":"","content":"<b>Beliar, the acceptance</b><br /> Rank 5 stygian entity. May or may not be a royal avatar of death itself... Shes very vauge about that, and enjoy implying contradictory things depending on the one she speaks to. <br /> <br /> More specifically shes the acceptance of death and loss. She is grief, and she is mourning. But she is also comfort in solace in knowing that death is an inevitable part of life for most mortals. <br /> For that reason shes a bitty enemy of those that cheat death. Cults, as well as cabals themed around her, are often taskes with hunting down those that trick death. Making her a potent antagonist for kindred, or others that did not die when they were &quot;supposed to.&quot;<br /> <br /> She does like to appear as a human, preferring to be mistaken for an archmage... this ofcourse causes some confusion for those having an encounter with her, as she appears to be bound by the supernal rules of summoning. But from her perspective, it is a lot simpler to act as a source of comfort and understanding when you dont look like a supernal creature beyond mortal comprehension. So when you encounter her, she will usually appear as a youngish woman, whos a bit on the pale side.. Only real tell is her eyes and mouth being black voids. <br /> <br /> The trials she sets before someone usually involves hunting down someone who defies death, and thus have gotten themselves on the list of enemies. Alternatively giving people the power to think they can truly bring back the dead. This always ends in people learning a dear lecture about along the lines of: &quot;things that are dead should not return.&quot;<br /> <br /> What she offers depend greatly on what the person seeks. She is compassionate, yes, and not unsympathetic to mortal tribulations. She will often grant boons involving power over the dead (Provided the user intents to put them to proper rest). Or boons relating to generally making other people able to aid others in accepting death... It really depends on what you need her to do, as she can be applied to the story as required by the Storyteller. <br /> <br /> Ban: Must hunt down and destroy anyone whos actively cheating death in her presence. <br /> Bane: Collected tears of someone mourning the loss of their child. <br /> <br /> <br /> She may sound like a great ally for most causes, but shes honestly more interesting to play out as an antagonist, or neutral party. Shes immensely powerful, but also immensely hard to get a hold on. In my campaign we have someone who lost a loved one, and is questing to bring him back. And in cases like that she works well as a understanding, but also sternly moralizing presence, that acts halfway as a mother figure trying to talk the PC to accept her grief. But also as a vast threat that promises to destroy the PC, if she ever reaches her goal.<br /> <br /> -... All in all, Im bending the rules a bit with this one (Mainly stuff about how she can interact with the mortal world regularly) But shes a ton of fun to pop in every so often!<br /> <br /> Also, she may or may not be inspired by &quot;Death&quot; from the Sandman comics by Niel Gaiman... But dont tell my players that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Decent storyteller. Poor Banjo player.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12373-sarner","name":"Sarner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12373_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T08:59:52-08:00","id":1159879,"title":"","content":"Interestingly we have a Beliar already. The Slave to Sloth.<br /> <br /> I like the write-up, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T09:44:40-08:00","id":1159891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153938-showcase-your-supernal-entities-goetia-spirits-and-ghosts-homebrew?p=1159879#post1159879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly we have a Beliar already. The Slave to Sloth.<br /> <br /> I like the write-up, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? Funny how the Maeljin have a tendency to ruin the best laid plans. <br /> Lucky for me none of my players have read a whole lot of Werewolf, so it could be a long while before they notice.. But the name could cause some confusion. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the heads up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Decent storyteller. Poor Banjo player.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12373-sarner","name":"Sarner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12373_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T14:00:26-08:00","id":1160963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>oeruli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153938-showcase-your-supernal-entities-goetia-spirits-and-ghosts-homebrew?p=1159280#post1159280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a good idea, Axelgear. Mechanically speaking, I think it could be done by taking the point of Extremism influence and moving it to either Information or Stress. Certainly this would be included among the many stresses of university life, but you do make a good point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vote Stress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T15:36:45-08:00","id":1160988,"title":"","content":"So, one of my players encountered a Seraphim that helped him during his Awakening. The chararacter's Virtue is Courage and his Vice is Corrupt. He's an Obrimos (Forces 3, Prime 2, Time 1)<br /> <br /> I'd like a traditional Seraphim that might pop back into the Chronicle at some point.<br /> <br /> Does anyone want to take a stab at creating it? Maybe Rank 3 or something.<br /> <br /> It originally appeared to help him find his sister because it was impressed by his courage in standing up to the mafia goons that kidnapped her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T17:20:54-08:00","id":1161017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153938-showcase-your-supernal-entities-goetia-spirits-and-ghosts-homebrew?p=1160988#post1160988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like a traditional Seraphim that might pop back into the Chronicle at some point.<br /> <br /> Does anyone want to take a stab at creating it? Maybe Rank 3 or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Traditionally you would go higher than Rank 3. In Christian belief they're the highest rank of angel. So do you want it more powerful and fitting tradition, or less and fitting your story?<br /> <br /> Or do you mean Seraphim as in Supernal entities and don't have much of a traditional appearance at all?<br /> <br /> Deionscribe converted one of the first edition idigam ones.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/fmgUbxb.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/939489-gamugur-the-unholy-host-2e#post939489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For most idigam, change is the bottom line. Even those that coalesce are constantly seeking new ways to change the world around them. A very few, though, have rejected change. They\u2019ve come to recognize that change for the sake of change leads to chaos. Gamugur is one of the rare idigam that values stability, and it has found that stability in the faith of humans.<br /> <br /> Contrary to modern iconography, angels weren\u2019t always described as humans with wings and halos. Always resistant to change, Gamugur has taken on the old-school appearance of an angel more in keeping with the descriptions found in the Old Testament or Dante\u2019s Divine Comedy. Each of Gamugur\u2019s three heads bears 33 never-blinking eyes, and its three mouths speak with one voice. Its body is sexless and has six arms and nine legs. Gamugur is borne aloft by blindingly white wings that are set in three rows on its back, and it is surrounded at all times by a nimbus of golden light.<br /> <br /> [For more information on this Idigam, see p. 139 of Night Horrors: Wolfsbane.]<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Gamugur, The Unholy Host</b></u><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 5<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Power 12, Finesse 15, Resistance 10<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Faith 3, Stability 4<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Gauntlet Breach, Image, Materialize, Reaching, Shadow Gateway, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Aggressive Meme, Emotional Aura, Fate Sense, Gauntlet Vision*, Implant Mission, Rapture, Resurrection**, Soul Snatch, Speed, Two Influence dots<br /> <b>Essence Shaping:</b> Essence Venom, Essence Void, Forge Servant (Claimed, Spawn***), One Million Eyes, Spirit Manipulation<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Bane-Salve, Divine Clay, Mind of God, The Light<br /> <br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 16<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 100<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 18<br /> <b>Size: </b>6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 20<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 20<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Gamugur cannot directly harm religious officials.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Communion wine blessed by the pastor of the congregation<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Divine Clay:</b> Gamugur may only reshape flesh to the form it had before an injury, due to its reluctance to alter even unhappy changes. Each success on a Power + Finesse roll downgrades injuries by one level, to a minimum of bashing damage.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Mind of God:</b> After communing with the stars, communicating with the minds of humans is child\u2019s play. Gamugur constantly hears the thoughts of humans as a kind of background murmur. By concentrating on a specific human, it can read that person\u2019s mind, down to their deepest, darkest secrets. Characters who would like to resist this kind of mental probing must first have some idea that Gamugur is reading their minds. Since the idigam often answers question before they are asked, however, this is pretty easy to guess at after a character has personally encountered the idigam at least once. Once a character knows (or guesses) that Gamugur is digging around in her head, she may roll Resolve + Composure (plus any supernatural resistance trait) vs. the idigam\u2019s Power + Finesse to resist.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>The Light:</b> While injury and disease represent a kind of change, reversing those changes through healing also alters a body. Instead of lowering itself to commit changes, Gamugur simply places disease and injury in a kind of stasis where they no longer hinder the inflicted. Using this power costs Gamugur three Essence. Wounds still heal at the normal rate, but diseases remain inactive for a number of days equal to successes in a Power + Finesse roll.<br /> <br /> * -- Gauntlet Vision is a combination of the 1E Numina, Material Vision and Spirit Vision<br /> ** -- Gamugur's Resurrection Numen does not suffer any penalties based on how much time has passed since the death. However, any and all revived individuals become Ascended.<br /> *** -- The Cherubs are the result of Gamugur's Forge Spawn power.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Or Here's Ulthoon. I'm not quite sure the power level of Trial 'victories' so I put down two.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ulthoon<br /> Rank: 3<br /> Power 9, Finesse 6, Resistance 8<br /> Corpus: 16<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Initiative: 14<br /> Defense: 6<br /> Speed: 30<br /> Size 8<br /> Ban: Must destroy its rank worth of objects larger than its Size per day or loses all Willpower.<br /> Bane: Weather-resonant beings of higher Rank<br /> Maximum Essence 20<br /> Numina: Air Elemental, Awe, Blast, Pathfinder, Seek, Speed, Telekinesis<br /> Manifestations: Twilight Form, <br /> Influences: Forces 3, Matter 3<br /> Virtue: Forceful<br /> Vice: Tempestuous<br /> <br /> Trial: To pass Ulthoon's trial one must defeat them in combat alone, but Ulthoon does not make this easy as it uses its speed and powers to cause as much chaos and destruction as possible. In return he can advise in ways to destroy any inanimate object, and has information about objects that have been destroyed purposefully or by natural disaster, not by aging. <br /> Description: It's a giant made of tornadoes, with a cyclone forming a rough torso and smaller funnels spawning off into crude arms. Two pale blue spots appear near its top and appear to act as eyes.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-20-2017, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T11:23:36-08:00","id":1161220,"title":"","content":"I dunno if it counts, because i didnt create them, i converted them.. but once upon a time, I made a final fantasy based supernal Summoner legacy (based on the choir of hashmallim) and as such converted a great number of final fantasy summons into supernal entities. Admittedly, I combined some, and as such many have extended titles like Golem the Titan, but.. If anyone is curious, I could share. <br /> <br /> For a brief example, Shiva is an Anachronism with Death who focuses on slowing enemies and hammering foes with her own speed. Her cold powers largely come from heat death. Spells include Axe Kick (time 1, perfect timing), Slow (time 3, chronos's curse), Queen's Sigh (death three, cold snap), Heavenly strike (death/time 3), Diamond Dust (death/time 4, agg damage plus lingering lvl 4 extreme environment).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T12:15:33-08:00","id":1161240,"title":"","content":"I was hoping for some ideas along the lines in the book:<br /> <br /> &quot;The manifest Angels are called Seraphim. Many resemble their resplendent<br /> and terrifying namesakes, complete with shining swords<br /> and magnificent wings.&quot;<br /> <br /> Rank 3 is probably powerful enough for something not crazy powerful that could upset my game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T12:35:24-08:00","id":1161249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153938-showcase-your-supernal-entities-goetia-spirits-and-ghosts-homebrew?p=1160988#post1160988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, one of my players encountered a Seraphim that helped him during his Awakening. The chararacter's Virtue is Courage and his Vice is Corrupt. He's an Obrimos (Forces 3, Prime 2, Time 1)<br /> <br /> I'd like a traditional Seraphim that might pop back into the Chronicle at some point.<br /> <br /> Does anyone want to take a stab at creating it? Maybe Rank 3 or something.<br /> <br /> It originally appeared to help him find his sister because it was impressed by his courage in standing up to the mafia goons that kidnapped her.</div> </div> </div> </div>This being hides behind its wings, clearly. Its voice is eternal truth, and its whispers creep around the listener, leaking from the open places between the wings like radiation.<br /> <br /> The angel says it has no name, only saying it represents Raziel and Beelzebub. The creature knows it's summoner well, and always contradicts them. For its own reasons obviously.<br /> <br /> It's secondary Arcana is Mind. It reads thoughts, and can vaguely guide them. It is a foil, it is an enabler, it is a judge, and it is a philosopher. It corrupts, it liberates, and it enlightens. But no human or mage would truly see it that way, because it corrupts good with evil and evil with good. By human moral standing, it is very confusing.<br /> <br /> It's trial consists of letting the being listen to you talk. It's smart, and will gladly discourse for days until it is satisfied. If angered, it's voice becomes the loudest, angriest parental figure and judge/king, capable of causing bashing damage. Because it is lesser, it will not usually kill, and many summoner who've lied or fought it's agenda have given up successfully and survived.<br /> <br /> It tends to rely on telepathy and sound based magic, but like any supernal or mage, it is capable of arcana based creative thaumaturgy, using lightning and fire, swaying minds outright.<br /> <br /> No idea on the specific mechanics of ban, bane, or stats. I'd say balanced, stat wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T13:38:56-08:00","id":1161262,"title":"","content":"Thanks. It's very cool. It might be too subtle for my game simply because the Obrimos in question is played by a 10 year old boy. I'm thankful for your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T13:52:50-08:00","id":1161266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1153938-showcase-your-supernal-entities-goetia-spirits-and-ghosts-homebrew?p=1161262#post1161262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. It's very cool. It might be too subtle for my game simply because the Obrimos in question is played by a 10 year old boy. I'm thankful for your help.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, lean more towards the sound side, yelling and whispering, and add the mind I'm only to expand on what that means. It's a lot like a parent that you can't tell if it means well or is angry at you. But you an very easily steer it towards secrets, runours, and anger, but more so portray it like a sound angel, whispering and yelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T23:30:49-08:00","id":1177788,"title":"","content":"I've been working on this supernal entity for an upcoming story. Feedback appreciated.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oriel&quot;<br /> Seraph of Prime, Death, and Fate<br /> Rank 5<br /> Oriel is the Angel of Destiny, the entity which knows the ultimate fate of every soul. Such a central and powerful symbol often masks its importance, claiming - perhaps not falsely - that it is merely a royal avatar of greater powers: a guide who can reveal, but not author, the strings of destiny. Only the most powerful of summoning rituals can reach this entity, although rumor has it that it can choose to appear for any summoning from Aether, Stygia, or forces of Fate to impart a revelation it deems necessay.<br /> <br /> The Ritual: first, and most obviously, the summoning must occur in an area rich with death resonance - on top of an Avernian Gate or Stygian verge is ideal. It may not, however, be performed in a personal sanctum: it must occur in a (theoretically) public place, open to any who seek answers about about the departed. Next, the ritual space must be prepared with appropriate symbols of fate, which demonstrate that the final destiny is shaped by the path one walks. Finally, to prove their understanding of death, the summoner must either kill a creature at the time and manner ordained by fate, or destroy one that has cheated death.<br /> Seers belonging to the cult of the Psychopomp who manage to gain a dot in Prelacy sometimes recieve secret invocations that can bypass some of the ritual requirements.<br /> <br /> The Trial: Any who seek Oriel's revelation must first confront truths about their own soul and the destinies which shape their past and future. This is a brief astral journey which most often takes the forms of death which have touched their life: those they've lost, or killed, or cannot bear to part with. Frequently, the vision includes choices the summoner has made which have already damned them, or shatters a hope they have been holding onto. For a rare few, it reveals the consequences of choices they have yet to make, particularly if it would cause widespread suffering. Many think of the trial as a boon in itself, but the angel imparts revelation designed to break the will and make them reconsider the hubris of their course of action.<br /> <br /> Boon: The chief boon imparted by Oriel is the most obvious reason to summon such an entity: it can reveal, and sometimes hasten, the fate of another soul. Such answers somehow manage to be both straightforwardly practical and so enigmatic as to obscure any truth. For example, it may reveal that a soul has been torn asunder, passed eternally behind the stars, has been written into the supernal, or has been reborn into a specific person. Many are told a list of people and locations without any context and no perceiveable trace of the soul in question; some consider this to mean &quot;no valid answer exists&quot;, while others believe that the soul is broken down and spread throughout the universe. If the soul is still in the Fallen World or any reachable realm, this is of course revealed - sometimes, even, with explanations of how it got there or how to reach it.<br /> Alternatively, if the soul in question is incorporated into the ritual, the summoner may ask Oriel to take it to its ultimate destiny early. Some ask this as a particularly final death, or in hopes of averting a coming tragedy. However, the angel only readily accepts if the soul has cheated death; for those whose time has not yet come, it will place a ban on the summoner to fulfill their remaining destiny in the mortal world - paying with every impact that soul would have on every other person. Consider this a combined spell of Forge Purpose (Prime 5) and Sworn Oaths (Fate 3), which grants supernatural insight into what impact must be recreated; the curse for breaking this Oath (or removing it) is that their own soul to be thrown into oblivion. The natural consequences, however, are that the Abyss will seep into the gaps of destiny, and other agents of Fate are called to mend those gaps as best they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 01-21-2018, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}